IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pa-hsc`

-- Pennsylvania Human Services Code, Article IV (public assistance) -- the seat of the applicant for, or recipient of, cash
-- assistance: a parent or caretaker applying for TANF cash assistance ("aid to families with dependent children" in the
-- Code), or an aged, blind or disabled person asking about the State supplement to SSI.
-- "Can I get cash assistance? Is anything stopping me? What counts as my resources and income? What work must I do, and
-- what happens if I don't? When can my grant be cut, and does it keep coming if I appeal?"
--
-- Every question calls the core in pa-hsc.l4; no rule is restated here. Each input is one fact the person can state.
-- The amount of a grant is not answered: the payment standards are in department regulations, not deposited.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Pennsylvania cash assistance -- the applicant's and recipient's questions`

§§ `Which programs`

@export Can I get general assistance cash from Pennsylvania on a given day?
GIVEN `the day I ask about` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want to know whether general assistance cash can be paid
GIVETH A `General assistance cash`
`Can I get general assistance cash` MEANS
    `general assistance cash on` `the day I ask about`

@export Am I eligible for Pennsylvania's State supplemental assistance (the State supplement to SSI) under s 432(2)?
GIVEN `I receive SSI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive federal Supplemental Security Income (SSI) for the aged, blind or disabled
      `I am aged, blind or disabled under the SSI rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are aged, blind or disabled as Title XVI of the Social Security Act defines it, even if you do not receive SSI
      `my income under the SSI rules` IS A NUMBER @desc Your monthly income in US dollars, counted under the SSI (Title XVI) standards and income disregards
      `the SSI payment plus the State supplement` IS A NUMBER @desc The combined monthly amount of the federal SSI payment and Pennsylvania's State supplemental assistance payment for someone in your situation, in US dollars (set by the department)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible for State supplemental assistance` IF
    `is eligible for State supplemental assistance` `I receive SSI` `I am aged, blind or disabled under the SSI rules` `my income under the SSI rules` `the SSI payment plus the State supplement`

§§ `Is anything barring me (ss 432, 432.22)`

DECLARE `What bars me` IS ONE OF
    `nothing in s 432(4), (5)(i), (9), (10) or s 432.22 bars me; the class, resource, income and work conditions still apply`
    `barred` HAS `the bar` IS A `Bar to assistance`

@export Is there anything in the Human Services Code that bars me from cash assistance?
GIVEN `I am a US citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a citizen of the United States
      `federal law requires assistance to me as a non-citizen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are not a citizen, whether federal law specifically requires that you be given assistance (for example as a qualified alien under 8 U.S.C. 1612); answer no if you are a citizen
      `I live in Pennsylvania` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a resident of Pennsylvania
      `I am an inmate of a public institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an inmate of a public institution, such as a prison or jail
      `I gave away property worth $500 or more in the last two years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the two years before you applied, you disposed of real or personal property worth $500 or more without getting fair value for it
      `I receive SSI` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you receive federal Supplemental Security Income (SSI)
      `I am aged, blind or disabled under the SSI rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are aged, blind or disabled as Title XVI of the Social Security Act defines it
      `my income under the SSI rules` IS A NUMBER @desc Your monthly income in US dollars counted under the SSI rules (0 if not relevant)
      `the SSI payment plus the State supplement` IS A NUMBER @desc The combined monthly federal SSI and State supplement amount for your situation, in US dollars (0 if not relevant)
      `I was sentenced for a felony or misdemeanor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been sentenced for a felony or misdemeanor
      `I have finished my time in custody` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If sentenced, whether you have completed the period of incarceration and any extension of it
      `I have paid all my fines, costs and restitution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If sentenced, whether you have paid all fines, costs and restitution
      `I am on parole or complying with my probation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If sentenced, whether you have been paroled, or are in compliance with all terms of your probation
      `I am keeping to an approved payment plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If sentenced, whether you are in compliance with an approved plan for paying your fines, costs and restitution
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `I have ever been married` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have ever been married
      `I am pregnant or caring for my child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are pregnant or caring for a dependent child
      `I live with a parent, guardian or adult relative, or in an approved supervised setting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live with your parent, legal guardian or another adult relative, or in an adult-supervised supportive living arrangement the department has approved
      `the department has granted me an exception for my and my child's health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an unmarried parent under 18 not living with an adult, whether the department has determined an exception would best serve your and your child's health and safety
      `I can show my parent or guardian cannot or should not house us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are an unmarried parent under 18, whether you can show your parent, guardian or other adult refuses or is unable to house you, threatens or has abused or neglected you or your child, or has misspent your assistance
GIVETH A `What bars me`
`Is anything barring me from cash assistance` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the bar to assistance` (`Person's circumstances` WITH
                `is a citizen of the United States`                                IS `I am a US citizen`
                `federal law specifically requires assistance to this non-citizen` IS `federal law requires assistance to me as a non-citizen`
                `is a resident of Pennsylvania`                                    IS `I live in Pennsylvania`
                `is an inmate of a public institution`                             IS `I am an inmate of a public institution`
                `disposed of property worth $500 or more without fair consideration within two years before applying` IS `I gave away property worth $500 or more in the last two years`
                `eligible for State supplemental assistance`                       IS `is eligible for State supplemental assistance` `I receive SSI` `I am aged, blind or disabled under the SSI rules` `my income under the SSI rules` `the SSI payment plus the State supplement`
                `barred by an unsatisfied sentence`                                IS `is barred by an unsatisfied sentence` `I was sentenced for a felony or misdemeanor` `I have finished my time in custody` `I have paid all my fines, costs and restitution` `I am on parole or complying with my probation` `I am keeping to an approved payment plan`
                `barred as a minor parent`                                         IS `is barred as a minor parent` `my age` `I have ever been married` `I am pregnant or caring for my child` `I live with a parent, guardian or adult relative, or in an approved supervised setting` `the department has granted me an exception for my and my child's health and safety` `I can show my parent or guardian cannot or should not house us`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `nothing in s 432(4), (5)(i), (9), (10) or s 432.22 bars me; the class, resource, income and work conditions still apply`
    WHEN JUST b THEN `barred` b

§§ `Resources and income (ss 432.5, 432.12)`

@export How much of my family's property counts as an "available resource" for cash assistance (s 432.5)?
GIVEN `people in my assistance group` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people are in your assistance group (the people whose needs are considered together, usually those living with you)
      `value of our other property` IS A NUMBER @desc The value in US dollars of your group's property other than your home, rings and heirlooms, clothing and toys, household furnishings and personal effects, work or rehabilitation equipment, retroactive assistance from a hearing, and one vehicle: for example cash, bank accounts, other vehicles and other real estate
      `equity in our one vehicle` IS A NUMBER @desc For one vehicle of your group, its fair market value (from a standard used-car guide) less what is still owed on its purchase price, in US dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of our property counts as a resource` MEANS
    `the available resource` `people in my assistance group` `value of our other property` `equity in our one vehicle`

-- The person asks this once for each member of the assistance group.
@export Does this member's gross income count when Pennsylvania decides my family's need for cash assistance (s 432.12(a))?
GIVEN `their age` IS A NUMBER @desc The member's age in years
      `they are a student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the member is a full-time or part-time student
      `they work full time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the member is employed full time
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this member's income count` IF
    `the member's gross income is considered` `their age` `they are a student` `they work full time`

@export How much of my family's monthly income counts when Pennsylvania decides whether we are eligible for cash assistance (s 432.12(a))?
GIVEN `we already receive cash assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your family already receives cash assistance (a recipient), rather than applying for the first time
      `our counted gross earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc The total monthly gross earned income (wages, self-employment) in US dollars of the members whose income counts
      `our counted other income` IS A NUMBER @desc The total monthly gross unearned income (for example child support, unemployment compensation, Social Security) in US dollars of the members whose income counts, leaving out income federal or state law excludes
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of our income counts for eligibility` MEANS
    `the income counted for eligibility` `we already receive cash assistance` `our counted gross earnings` `our counted other income`

@export If my family has lived in Pennsylvania less than twelve months, what is the most cash assistance we can get (s 432(5)(ii))?
GIVEN `months we have lived in Pennsylvania` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months you have lived in Pennsylvania
      `the most our previous state would pay` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum monthly assistance payment your family would have received in the state you lived in before, in US dollars
      `the most Pennsylvania pays a family like ours` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum monthly assistance payment available to your family in Pennsylvania, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The most cash assistance we can get` MEANS
    `the most cash assistance can be` `months we have lived in Pennsylvania` `the most our previous state would pay` `the most Pennsylvania pays a family like ours`

§§ `Work requirements (ss 405.1, 432.3)`

@export What work requirement do I have to meet to get or keep cash assistance (s 405.1)?
GIVEN `I have a verified disability that stops me working` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a physician or psychologist has assessed you, in writing in the department's form, as having a physical or mental disability that temporarily or permanently precludes any employment or work-related activity
      `I care for a child under six and have no child care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a specified relative caring for a child under six for whom no alternate child care is available
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in years
      `hours I work per week` IS A NUMBER @desc The average number of hours a week you are employed
      `months of cash assistance I have had` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of cash assistance you have received in total, counting interrupted months
GIVETH A `Work requirement`
`What work requirement applies to me` MEANS
    `the work requirement that applies` (`may be exempt from the work requirements` `I have a verified disability that stops me working` `I care for a child under six and have no child care` `my age`) `hours I work per week` `months of cash assistance I have had`

-- Situation: only where the person has failed a work requirement without good cause.
@export If I fail a work requirement without good cause, how long am I disqualified, and is it only me or my whole family (s 432.3)?
GIVEN `which time this is` IS A NUMBER @desc Whether this is your first, second or third (or later) violation: 1, 2 or 3
      `months of cash assistance I had had when it happened` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of cash assistance you had received, in total, when the reason for the disqualification occurred
GIVETH A `Disqualification outcome`
`What disqualification do I face` MEANS
    `the disqualification` `which time this is` `months of cash assistance I had had when it happened`

@export If I am disqualified for failing a work requirement, what is the earliest day the disqualification can end?
GIVEN `the day the disqualification began` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the disqualification
      `which time this is` IS A NUMBER @desc Whether this is your first, second or third (or later) violation: 1, 2 or 3
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`The earliest day my disqualification can end` MEANS
    `the earliest day a disqualification can end` `the day the disqualification began` `which time this is`

-- Situation: only where a disability exemption has ended.
@export My disability exemption from the work requirements has ended: how many days do I have to start meeting them (s 405.1(a.4)(1))?
GIVEN `months of cash assistance when my condition ended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of cash assistance you had received, in total, when the condition that exempted you ceased
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How long do I have to start the work requirements` MEANS
    `days to comply after a disability exemption ends` `months of cash assistance when my condition ended`

§§ `Notice and appeal (ss 432.17, 423)`

-- Situation: only where the person has been told their grant will be cut, stopped or suspended.
@export The department has mailed me notice that it will cut or stop my cash assistance: what is the earliest day the change can take effect (s 432.17)?
GIVEN `the day the notice was mailed` IS A DATE @desc The day the department mailed the notice of its intended action
GIVETH A DATE
`When can the cut take effect` MEANS
    `the earliest day the change can take effect` `the day the notice was mailed`

@export If I appeal a decision to cut or stop my cash assistance, does my assistance keep coming until the hearing decision (s 423(a))?
GIVEN `I already receive assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are already receiving assistance
      `I asked for a hearing within the timely notice period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you requested a fair hearing within the timely notice period (the ten days between the mailing of the notice and the change)
      `the only issue is the law or policy itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only issue in the appeal is a State or Federal law or policy, or a change in it, rather than the facts of your case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my assistance continue pending the hearing` IF
    `assistance continues until the hearing decision` `I already receive assistance` `I asked for a hearing within the timely notice period` `the only issue is the law or policy itself`
